<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>What Comes in the DQ Chicken Strip Basket</h2>
  <p>Every Chicken Strip Basket at <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a> includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Chicken strips</strong> — 4 crispy whole white-meat strips, hand-battered and cooked to order</li>
    <li><strong>Seasoned fries</strong> — A full side order of crispy golden fries</li>
    <li><strong>Texas toast</strong> — One thick slice of buttery toasted bread</li>
    <li><strong>Dipping sauce</strong> — Your choice of Country Gravy, Ranch, Honey Mustard, BBQ, or Sweet &amp; Sour</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Dipping Sauce Guide — Which to Choose</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
    <thead><tr><th>Sauce</th><th>Flavor Profile</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Country Gravy</strong></td><td>Creamy, savory, peppery</td><td>Traditional DQ experience — most popular</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Ranch</strong></td><td>Cool, creamy, herby</td><td>Classic pairing, second most popular</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Honey Mustard</strong></td><td>Sweet and tangy</td><td>Lighter alternative to gravy</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>BBQ Sauce</strong></td><td>Smoky and sweet</td><td>Pairs well with plain strips</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Sweet &amp; Sour</strong></td><td>Light, fruit-forward</td><td>Guests who prefer a lighter dip</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h2>Sauced Basket Options — Worth the $0.50 Upgrade?</h2>
  <p>For $10.49 (a $0.50 premium over the plain 4-Piece), you can order a Sauced Basket with the sauce tossed directly onto the strips before serving:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Honey BBQ Basket</strong> — Sweet honey BBQ tossed on the strips, fries included</li>
    <li><strong>Parmesan Garlic Basket</strong> — Rich Parmesan garlic sauce on the strips</li>
    <li><strong>FlameThrower® Basket</strong> — Spicy FlameThrower sauce on the strips</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Opting for a tossed, sauced basket is well worth the extra fifty cents if you prefer bold, edge-to-edge flavor. Rather than relying on a small dipping cup that only coats the surface, the tossed version ensures tangy Honey BBQ or spicy FlameThrower glaze penetrates every crunchy ridge and crevice of the hand-breaded chicken.</p>
  <h2>4-Piece vs. 6-Piece — Which to Order</h2>
  <p>For an average lunch or dinner, the 4-Piece basket ($9.99) is perfectly portioned for one adult. If you bring a serious appetite or plan on sharing with a friend, upgrading to the <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-6pc">6-Piece basket</a> ($13.49) adds two more hearty strips and lowers your cost per tenderloin.</p>
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How many calories in the DQ Chicken Strip Basket?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The complete 4-Piece basket, including fries and grilled Texas toast, contains around 1,000 calories. The exact count varies slightly depending on which dipping sauce you select.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What dipping sauce comes with the DQ Chicken Strip Basket?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Every basket comes with your choice of one dipping cup: Country Gravy (the iconic classic), Ranch, Honey Mustard, Smokey BBQ, or Sweet &amp; Sour.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can I get a Chicken Strip Basket without fries?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The basket comes standard with crispy fries and Texas toast. While you can request no fries when ordering, the platter is priced as a bundled meal.</div></div></div></div>
  <p style="margin-top:32px;">For the complete DQ menu including all categories and deals, visit <a href="/"><strong>The Queen Dairy Menu</strong></a>.</p>
